{"notes":[{"content":{"venue":{"value":"ICRA 2026"},"venueid":{"value":"OpenReview.net/Public_Article"},"paperhash":{"value":"shao|symskill_symbol_and_skill_coinvention_for_dataefficient_and_reactive_longhorizon_manipulation"},"html":{"value":"https://ras.papercept.net/conferences/conferences/ICRA26/program/ICRA26_ContentListWeb_4.html#webt1_08"},"title":{"value":"SymSkill: Symbol and Skill Co-Invention for Data-Efficient and Reactive Long-Horizon Manipulation"},"authors":{"value":[{"fullname":"Yifei Shao","username":"","institutions":[{"name":"University of Pennsylvania"}]},{"fullname":"Yuchen Zheng","username":"","institutions":[{"name":"University of Pennsylvania"}]},{"fullname":"Sunan Sun","username":"","institutions":[{"name":"University of Pennsylvania"}]},{"fullname":"Pratik Chaudhari","username":"","institutions":[{"name":"University of Pennsylvania"}]},{"fullname":"Vijay Kumar","username":"","institutions":[{"name":"University of Pennsylvania"}]},{"fullname":"Nadia Figueroa","username":"","institutions":[{"name":"University of Pennsylvania"}]}]}},"tmdate":1788890297658,"tcdate":1788890297658,"writers":["~","OpenReview.net/Public_Article/Manual_Import","OpenReview.net/Support"],"signatures":["OpenReview.net/Support"],"forum":"AuBWVCnNmd","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","number":706,"cdate":1788890297658,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["OpenReview.net/Public_Article/Manual_Import/-/Record"],"mdate":1788890297658,"domain":"OpenReview.net/Public_Article","id":"AuBWVCnNmd","version":2},{"content":{"venue":{"value":"CoRL 2025 Workshop LEAP (Rolling)"},"pdf":{"value":"/pdf/603915125c11d3e26fbcad7815bcb89a2357c1b7.pdf"},"keywords":{"value":["Symbol and Skill Co-Invention","real-time TAMP","Imitation Learning","Human-Centered Robots","Long-Horizon Manipulation","Dynamical Systems"]},"venueid":{"value":"robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling"},"paperhash":{"value":"shao|symskill_symbol_and_skill_coinvention_for_dataefficient_and_realtime_longhorizon_manipulation"},"authorids":{"value":["~Yifei_Simon_Shao1","~Yuchen_Zheng2","~Sunan_Sun1","~Nadia_Figueroa1"]},"abstract":{"value":"Multi-step manipulation in dynamic environments remains challenging. Two major families of methods fail in distinct ways: (i) imitation learning (IL) is reactive but lacks \\emph{compositional generalization}, as monolithic policies do not decide which skill to reuse when scenes change; (ii) classical task-and-motion planning (TAMP) offers compositionality but has prohibitive \\emph{planning latency}, preventing real-time failure recovery.\nWe introduce \\texttt{SymSkill}, a unified learning framework that combines the benefits of IL and TAMP, allowing compositional generalization and failure recovery in real-time. Offline, \\texttt{SymSkill} jointly learns predicates, operators, and skills directly from unlabeled and unsegmented demonstrations. At execution time, upon specifying a conjunction of one or more learned predicates, \\texttt{SymSkill} uses a symbolic planner to compose and reorder learned skills to achieve the symbolic goals, while performing recovery at both the motion and symbolic levels in real time. Coupled with a compliant controller, \\texttt{SymSkill} enables safe and uninterrupted execution under human and environmental disturbances.\nIn RoboCasa simulation, \\texttt{SymSkill} can execute 12 single-step tasks with 85\\% success rate. Without additional data, it composes these skills into multi-step plans requiring up to 6 skill recompositions, recovering robustly from execution failures. On a real Franka robot, we demonstrate \\texttt{SymSkill}, learning from 5 minutes of unsegmented and unlabeled play data, is capable of performing multiple tasks simply by goal specifications. \nThe source code and additional analysis can be found on https://sites.google.com/view/symskill"},"_bibtex":{"value":"@inproceedings{\nshao2026symskill,\ntitle={SymSkill: Symbol and Skill Co-Invention for Data-Efficient and Real-Time Long-Horizon Manipulation},\nauthor={Yifei Simon Shao and Yuchen Zheng and Sunan Sun and Nadia Figueroa},\nbooktitle={3rd CoRL Workshop on Learning Effective Abstractions for Planning (Rolling)},\nyear={2026},\nurl={https://openreview.net/forum?id=sJXvdItBLT}\n}"},"title":{"value":"SymSkill: Symbol and Skill Co-Invention for Data-Efficient and Real-Time Long-Horizon Manipulation"},"authors":{"value":["Yifei Simon Shao","Yuchen Zheng","Sunan Sun","Nadia Figueroa"]}},"tmdate":1769976372858,"pdate":1769976372443,"tcdate":1757116596237,"writers":["robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling","robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling/Submission16/Authors"],"signatures":["robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling/Submission16/Authors"],"forum":"sJXvdItBLT","license":"CC BY 4.0","number":16,"cdate":1757116596237,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling/-/Submission","robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling/-/Post_Submission","robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling/Submission16/-/Camera_Ready","robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling/-/Edit"],"mdate":1769976372858,"odate":1769976372443,"domain":"robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Workshop/LEAP_Rolling","id":"sJXvdItBLT","version":2}],"count":2}